Now let me look at the `node_min_byte_len` function for the BAG_IF_ELSE case more carefully. I see the bug now:

```c
case BAG_IF_ELSE:
    {
        OnigLen elen;

        len = node_min_byte_len(NODE_BODY(node), env);
        if (IS_NOT_NULL(en->te.Then))
            len += node_min_byte_len(en->te.Then, env);
        if (IS_NOT_NULL(en->te.Else))
            elen = node_min_byte_len(en->te.Else, env);
        else elen = 0;

        if (elen < len) len = elen;
    }
```

Wait, `elen` is declared but not initialized. If `en->te.Else` is not NULL, `elen` gets set. If it IS NULL, `elen = 0`. So that seems fine.

Let me look at the `node_min_byte_len` for NODE_BACKREF more carefully. The issue is that `mem_env[backs[i]].mem_node` could be NULL or could point to freed memory.

Let me look at how `mem_env` is set up and when `mem_node` gets freed:

